@.s747 = private unnamed_addr constant [793 x i8] c"    {\22code\22: \22E0124\22, \22title\22: \22A conversion or its 'else' is written wrongly\22, \22match\22: [\22after 'as'\22, \22needs a value that may be missing\22, \22block of a 'let' must leave\22], \22text\22: \22'as' converts to int, float or string. 'else' after a let, and 'if (let ...)', take a value\5Cnthat may be missing: a conversion that can fail (to int or to float), an index or field read,\5Cnfind, index_of, last_index_of or open. The 'else' block of a let must leave with return, break\5Cnor continue, because after the let the name must hold a value.\22, \22example\22: \22func f(s) \5C{\5Cn    let n = s as int else \5C{\5Cn        print(\5C\22not a number\5C\22)\5Cn    }\5Cn    return n\5Cn}\5Cnprint(f(\5C\224\5C\22))\22, \22fix\22: \22Give a value that may be missing, such as s as int or m[key], and end the 'else' block with\5Cnreturn, break or continue.\22},\00"
@.s748 = private unnamed_addr constant [941 x i8] c"    {\22code\22: \22E0125\22, \22title\22: \22A named argument does not fit the call\22, \22match\22: [\22is named twice\22, \22cannot come after a named one\22, \22has no parameter\22, \22by position and by name\22, \22Named arguments go in the order\22, \22needs a value for\22, \22has only\22, \22cannot skip\22, \22takes no named arguments\22, \22Named arguments need a function\22], \22text\22: \22A call can name its arguments, greet(\5C\22Ann\5C\22, greeting: \5C\22Hi\5C\22). The named ones come after the\5Cnpositional ones and in the order of the parameters, each parameter is given once, and every\5Cnparameter without a default gets a value. The function must be known when the program is built:\5Cnone declared with func (and not assigned elsewhere), a template, or a builtin that has names.\22, \22example\22: \22func greet(name, greeting = \5C\22Hello\5C\22) \5C{\5Cn    return greeting + name\5Cn}\5Cnprint(greet(\5C\22Ann\5C\22, greting: \5C\22Hi\5C\22))\22, \22fix\22: \22Use the names the message lists, in their order, or pass the arguments by position.\22},\00"
