@.s777 = private unnamed_addr constant [522 x i8] c"    {\22code\22: \22E0460\22, \22title\22: \22An unsafe rule was broken\22, \22match\22: [\22unsafe\22, \22alloc()\22, \22free()\22, \22box\22, \22pointer\22, \22ptr_add()\22, \22address_of\22, \22defer()\22, \22double free\22, \22use-after-free\22], \22text\22: \22Raw memory is only allowed inside unsafe blocks, and the ten rules there are checked: no\5Cnuse after free, no double free, no pointer that outlives its block, and every alloc() freed.\22, \22example\22: \22unsafe \5C{ let p = alloc(8) }\22, \22fix\22: \22Free what you allocate, keep pointers inside their block, and read docs/unsafe.md.\22},\00"
